; Printing an all-zero balance with print() or eval must leave the
; alignment of the report's output alone: later --prepend-width columns
; and stats counts rely on its default right alignment.
;
; Unless a width is set for it, Ledger writes a balance straight to the
; report's output instead of first laying it out in a buffer of its own,
; which was costly when done for every value.  A balance with no non-zero
; component prints the placeholder "0", padded with spaces like every
; amount rather than by setting a width and an alignment on the output: a
; width lapses after one write, but an alignment stays in force.  print()
; and eval write to the report's output without right-aligning, so a left
; alignment left behind there would turn every later prepended account
; name and stats count left-aligned.  The alignment is what it was when
; Ledger laid out every balance in a buffer of its own.

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Dollars      10 USD
    Assets:Euros         5 EUR
    Equity:Dollars     -10 USD
    Equity:Euros        -5 EUR

2024/01/02 Coffee
    Expenses:Coffee      3 USD
    Assets:Dollars

; An unfiltered register's running total returns to zero after each
; transaction; with two commodities it is a balance whose components are
; all zero, which print(total) shows as "0".  The prepended account names
; stay right-aligned after it, including on the Coffee line, whose own
; total is not zero.

test reg --prepend-format '%(account)' --prepend-width 30 -d 'print(total)'
10 USD
                Assets:Dollars24-Jan-01 Opening               Assets:Dollars               10 USD       10 USD
5 EUR
10 USD
                  Assets:Euros                                Assets:Euros                  5 EUR        5 EUR
                                                                                                        10 USD
5 EUR
                Equity:Dollars                                Equity:Dollars              -10 USD        5 EUR
0
                  Equity:Euros                                Equity:Euros                 -5 EUR            0
3 USD
               Expenses:Coffee24-Jan-02 Coffee                Expenses:Coffee               3 USD        3 USD
0
                Assets:Dollars                                Assets:Dollars               -3 USD            0
end test

; The same through stats, printing a constant zero balance from the limit
; predicate (eval prints a value through the same path).  Adding the
; negated amounts keeps a balance of zero components, where subtracting
; them would simplify it to the number 0.  The counts stay right-aligned
; in their six-column fields.

test stats --now 2030/06/15 -l 'print(1 USD + 1 EUR + -1 USD + -1 EUR)'
0
0
0
0
0
0
Time period: 24-Jan-01 to 24-Jan-02 (2 days)

  Files these postings came from:
    $FILE

  Unique payees:               2
  Unique accounts:             5

  Number of postings:          6 (3 per day)
  Uncleared postings:          6

  Days since last post:     2356
  Posts in last 7 days:        0
  Posts in last 30 days:       0
  Posts seen this month:       0
end test

; The placeholder itself is padded to its column like any amount:
; right-justified in the register's total column above, left-justified
; here.

test reg --format '[%(justify(total, 8))] %(account)\n' -d 'account =~ /^Equity/'
[5 EUR   ] Equity:Dollars
[0       ] Equity:Euros
end test
